{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22609 - PROTEIN:5793",
  "verbalization": "NRF2 activator Geopyxin F is implicated in the activation of SNU-387, a compound that is subsequently targeted by multiple downstream molecules, including 10,22-Dihydroxy-7,7,18,18-tetramethyl-8,13,17-trioxapentacyclo[12.8.0.03,12.04,9.016,21]docosa-1(22),3(12),4(9),10,14,16(21),19-heptaen-2-one and S-ethylcysteine zwitterion. All of these entities ultimately target Hepatocyte, suggesting a potential pathway where Geopyxin F may influence cellular processes through the activation of SNU-387, which in turn modulates the activity of other molecules that ultimately affect hepatocyte function. The evidence suggests a possible mechanism involving the activation of a signaling cascade that leads to changes in hepatocyte behavior, though the exact molecular pathways remain to be fully elucidated.",
